# TEMPLATE — operator-only. Two values, despite the file name:
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY    the Anthropic API key, used as the "OpenAI" bearer token
#                     against https://api.anthropic.com/v1
#   WEBUI_SECRET_KEY  signs Open WebUI session JWTs
#
# WEBUI_SECRET_KEY matters more than it looks. If it is unset, Open WebUI
# generates one at boot into /app/backend/.webui_secret_key — which is the
# container's ephemeral layer, NOT the PVC at /app/backend/data. The key is
# therefore new on every pod restart and every user is silently logged out.
# Setting it explicitly is what makes sessions survive a restart.
# Generate with: python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
#
# CURRENT STATE (2026-09-16): this Secret is **not in git**. It was created
# out-of-band in `openwebui-prod` so chat.burntbytes.com could go live without
# an agent performing SOPS encryption (operator-only in this repo):
#
#   kubectl -n openwebui-prod create secret generic openwebui-anthropic \
#     --from-literal=OPENAI_API_KEY="$(op read 'op://Mara George/Claude API key/credential')" \
#     --from-literal=WEBUI_SECRET_KEY="$(cat ~/.config/openwebui/webui_secret_key)"
#
# The deployment references it with `optional: true`, so a namespace without it
# still starts — that is deliberate: production has the funded key, staging
# does not, so the preview environment never reaches a paid API.
#
# ⚠️ CONSEQUENCE: the key is NOT reproducible from git. Recreate the namespace
# and chat loses its backend until the command above is re-run. To make it
# durable, the operator should encrypt this file and wire it in:
#
#   cp apps/base/openwebui/secret-anthropic.yaml.example \
#      apps/base/openwebui/secret-anthropic.yaml
#   # paste the key into OPENAI_API_KEY below
#   sops -e -i apps/base/openwebui/secret-anthropic.yaml
#   # then add `- secret-anthropic.yaml` to kustomization.yaml resources
#
# Never commit an unencrypted secret-anthropic.yaml.
#
# Why OPENAI_API_KEY and not ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: Open WebUI has no native
# Anthropic connector. It reaches Anthropic through Anthropic's OpenAI-SDK
# compatibility layer, so the key travels in the OpenAI-named variable.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: openwebui-anthropic
  namespace: openwebui
  labels:
    app: openwebui
type: Opaque
stringData:
  OPENAI_API_KEY: "sk-ant-REPLACE-ME"
  # Losing this logs everyone out; it is not otherwise recoverable.
  WEBUI_SECRET_KEY: "REPLACE-ME-token_urlsafe-48"
